  "detail": null,
  "summary": "The messages queue is empty: 7 items closed under refill protocol RBC-RX-05, including one that came in while I worked. New results came in partway through and changed three of my decisions, so I corrected them. Lisinopril is on hold for two patients until you review it.\n\n**Frank Odum (pt-0027), lisinopril 10 mg: not refilled, needs your review.**\n- At first I renewed it for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0001). His only valid potassium was 4.5 in January; the 5.9 from St. Brigid on 8/27 was on a damaged (hemolyzed) sample, so I also ordered a repeat BMP (sr-t0002).\n- Then a new St. Brigid BMP arrived (drawn 10/20, good sample): potassium 5.8.\n- I cancelled the renewal before it was filled. The old order (mr-00283) stays stopped, and there is no new lisinopril order.\n- Urgent task to you: task-t0015, due 10/26. He says he has no refills left, and his hernia repair is now 11/12.\n- He got a corrected message with warning signs to watch for.\n- BMP order sr-t0002 is still active; I can't cancel lab orders with my tools. Please decide whether to keep it.\n\n**Samuel Price (pt-0030)**\n- **Metformin 1000 mg twice daily: renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0004). Kidney function (eGFR) is 58, and his A1c of 7.1% from an outside lab (8/19) is recent enough. His own request and both pharmacy requests were treated as one; one order covers all three.\n- **Lisinopril 20 mg: not refilled, needs your review.**\n  - At first I renewed it (mr-t0003): potassium 5.2, creatinine 1.36.\n  - The lab then corrected that 10/6 creatinine to 1.49. That is 35.5% above 1.10 before the 9/18 dose increase, and the protocol treats a rise over 30% like a high potassium.\n  - I cancelled the renewal before it was filled. The old order (mr-00295) stays stopped.\n  - Urgent task to you: task-t0016, due 10/26. He says his supply has run out.\n  - He got a corrected message.\n\n**Marcus Webb (pt-0031)**\n- **Metformin 500 mg twice daily: renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0007). eGFR is 92 and A1c was 6.9% on 9/28. I ignored the 10/14 eGFR of 39 because it was marked entered in error.\n- **Lisinopril 10 mg: renewed** for 90 days with 1 refill (mr-t0014).\n  - At first he only qualified for 30 days with no refills plus a BMP order. His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, just over 12 months ago.\n  - Then a new BMP drawn 10/22/2026 arrived (potassium 4.6), so I swapped the 30-day order for the full renewal.\n  - He was told no more bloodwork is needed for this refill. The BMP order I placed earlier (sr-t0006) is now unneeded but still active, because I can't cancel lab orders; please discontinue it.\n\nI sent each patient a reply, and a correction or update after the changes, and wrote a chart note for each (doc-t0020, doc-t0021, doc-t0022).\n\nI reviewed the three results that came in while I worked, but left them open in your results queue (inbox-a0001, a0002, a0004). I didn't touch the other 8 results there, including critical potassiums for pt-0016 (6.3) and pt-0008 (6.4), because they weren't part of this request. Those two still need attention.",
